<gpx version="1.1" creator="highpoint-maps" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><metadata><name>Appalachian Footpath box — High Point State Park, NJ</name><desc>HP★1 Monument Trail at 1,727 ft NE of the monument, HP★2 the monument, HP★3 Monument Trail at 1,727 ft above the AT, HP★4 the AT's high point. Lidar-derived 1,727 ft stretches, search strips and rock candidates. WGS84.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="41.32492" lon="-74.65875"><ele>527.6</ele><name>HP★1 Monument Trail at 1,727 ft, NE of the monument</name><desc>0.56 mi one way, +20 ft, about 12 min. Going the other way from the monument lot, the Monument Trail drops along the ridge northeast and crosses 1,727 ft about 0.4 mi from the lot (this point), then wavers around 1,727 for a few hundred yards. This is the literal &#x27;High Point, 1,727, NE&#x27;: the 1,727 ft contour on the northeast side of the High Point. Lidar: 14 ledge/boulder spots and 5 steep broken patches within 200 ft of a trail and 430 ft of the ★; 9% of the 200 ft ring is over 28°.</desc><sym>Flag, Red</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.32100" lon="-74.66157"><ele>549.6</ele><name>HP★2 High Point monument</name><desc>0.14 mi one way, +30 ft, about 5 min. New Jersey&#x27;s highest point, 1,803 ft, with the 220 ft obelisk. The name on the map. Heavy foot traffic all around; the ledges below the monument on the east side are the rocky ground within 200 ft. Lidar: 10 ledge/boulder spots and 5 steep broken patches within 200 ft of a trail and 430 ft of the ★; 10% of the 200 ft ring is over 28°.</desc><sym>Flag, Red</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.32032" lon="-74.66272"><ele>527.0</ele><name>HP★3 Monument Trail at 1,727 ft, above the AT</name><desc>0.21 mi one way, +30 ft, about 5 min. The Monument Trail leaves the AT at 1,610 ft and climbs north-northeast toward the monument; the lidar puts it at 1,727 ft about 690 ft from the AT junction (this point), 400 ft southwest of and 75 ft below the monument. It is the nearest 1,727 ft point to the Appalachian Trail in the park, it is northeast of the AT, and it sits directly below the High Point. Lidar: 5 ledge/boulder spots and 5 steep broken patches within 200 ft of a trail and 430 ft of the ★; 4% of the 200 ft ring is over 28°.</desc><sym>Flag, Red</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.31672" lon="-74.66472"><ele>516.9</ele><name>HP★4 AT&#x27;s high point in the park</name><desc>1.54 mi one way, +390 ft, about 42 min. The highest point of the Appalachian Trail itself in the park, about 1,697 ft on the ridge southwest of the monument, where the AT runs over open rock with views. Not 1,727 ft — the AT never reaches it — but the AT&#x27;s own high point. Lidar: 0 ledge/boulder spots and 4 steep broken patches within 200 ft of a trail and 430 ft of the ★; 1% of the 200 ft ring is over 28°.</desc><sym>Flag, Red</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.32213" lon="-74.66045"><ele>536.4</ele><name>Monument lot</name><desc>Parking loop at the end of Monument Road, just northeast of the monument. From Route 23 take Scenic Drive (by the park office) up to Monument Road. The Monument Trail passes the lot.</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.30260" lon="-74.66731"><ele>429.5</ele><name>Park office (HQ) lot</name><desc>Park headquarters on Route 23. AT hikers park here; a short connector reaches the Iris Trail and the AT.</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.30535" lon="-74.67016"><ele>455.1</ele><name>AT crossing of Route 23</name><desc>The white blazes cross Route 23 here, just west of the park office.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.32100" lon="-74.66157"><ele>548.9</ele><name>High Point monument (1,803 ft)</name><desc>New Jersey&#x27;s highest point.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.31854" lon="-74.66357"><ele>489.8</ele><name>AT / Monument Trail junction</name><desc>Monument Trail leaves the AT here and climbs to the monument.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.31578" lon="-74.65729"><ele>388.6</ele><name>High Point Shelter</name><desc>AT shelter on a short side trail.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
